      "content": "XAUT vs $PAXG vs $XAG: Two Gold Tokens and Silver After a Red Day\nToday's move\nGold: about $4,024, down 1.1%\nSilver ($XAG): about $52.4, down 2.9%\n$XAUT and $PAXG: both down about 0.6%, tracking gold\n\nWhat separates them\n$XAUT (Tether Gold): the larger gold token, with a market cap near $3B\n\n$PAXG (Pax Gold): the smaller one, near $1.8B, also backed by one ounce of gold per token\n\n$XAG: silver, which moves more than gold in both directions\n\nThe bigger picture\nGold is about 28% below its January record\nSilver is down about 26% this year and 13% in the last month\n\nThe gold-to-silver ratio sits near 77, so silver has been the weaker of the two\n\nWhat I'm watching: the next US inflation data (PCE), since rate expectations drive both metals. The gold tokens give gold exposure on-chain, while $XAG is the higher-volatility way to trade the same theme.\n\nYour pick: $XAUT, $PAXG or $XAG into the next data release? Tell me why.\n$XAUTUSDT $PARTIUSDT #ByXIMPACT #IMPACTbyTrade ",
